The premise says the earthquake occurred on Thursday, 28 December. Thursday is the fifth day of the week if Monday is day one (Monday=1, Tuesday=2, Wednesday=3, Thursday=4, Friday=5) — but Thursday is the fourth day under Monday-start counting, and the fifth under Sunday-start counting (Sunday=1, Monday=2, Tuesday=3, Wednesday=4, Thursday=5). Under the standard ISO convention (Monday=1), Thursday is day 4, so the hypothesis contradicts the premise. Under the Sunday-start convention, it is entailed.

The most common convention in everyday and ISO usage is Monday-start, making the hypothesis a contradiction.

